        "original_id": "ed66570a-e438-5416-8c00-1eac9164e4a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Whit Alexander, Richard Tait, Karen Seyfarth, Andreas Seyfarth, Gary Baseman\n- Products: Cranium, Thurn and Taxis, Teacher's Pet\n- Companies: Hans im Glück, Rio Grande Games, ABC, Disney\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Whit Alexander and Richard Tait created the party game Cranium after Richard Tait spent a weekend playing games with another family and identified a need for a game using a variety of skills.\n- In 2006, Karen Seyfarth and Andreas Seyfarth designed the board game Thurn and Taxis.\n- In 2006, Hans im Glück published Thurn and Taxis in German as \"Thurn und Taxis,\" and Rio Grande Games published it in English.\n- Gary Baseman created the Emmy-winning ABC and Disney cartoon series Teacher's Pet.\n- Gary Baseman was the artistic designer of Cranium, which is described as a popular award-winning board game.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
